- op: create  # 9957
  at: '2026-09-21T01:01:07Z'  # 9957
  by: agent  # 9957
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9957
  clock: 1  # 9957
  nonce: '9957'  # 9957
  data:  # 9957
    kind: invariant  # 9957
    title: "Symbol.signature declares 'consumers display, never branch on the value itself' while 8 shipped consumers parse and branch on it — ADR-0051's retired defect, one field over"  # 9957
    status: needs_human_review  # 9957
    priority: 2  # 9957
    parent:  # 9957
    tags:  # 9957
    - analysis_quality  # 9957
    isbefore: []  # 9957
    duplicate_of: []  # 9957
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9957
    pr_ref:  # 9957
    description: "FOUND while implementing WI-fihun's cure (2), which needs a member's declared type and has nowhere else to read it.\n\n`Symbol.signature` in ir.py:652 declares:\n\n    signature: Optional[str] = None  # axis: free-text — callable signature string in source-language grammar; consumers display, never branch on the value itself.\n\nTHE CLAUSE IS FALSE, and has been for a long time. Consumers that parse the VALUE and branch on what they find, all shipped:\n\n    csharp.py:442    _extract_csharp_return_type_name(resolved_sym.signature) -> resolves a class\n    csharp.py:1650   _count_signature_params(c.signature) == arg_count -> overload selection\n    py.py:5881       _extract_return_type_name(assigned_class.signature) -> seeds var_types\n    kotlin.py:1587, kotlin.py:1724, js_ts.py:5309, dart.py:817 -> same return-type shape\n    linkers/jackson_dispatch.py:294  _get_signature(sym) -> parameter-ARITY filtering\n\nThat is at least 8 branch sites across a core linker and five analyzers, and they are not incidental: return-type inference is how a variable gets a type at all in py.py, which is the machinery WI-fihun's cure (1) extends.\n\nTHIS IS ADR-0051's DEFECT, ONE FIELD OVER. ADR-0051 retired the axis on `ExternalRef.module_path`, whose declaration read almost verbatim -- \"consumers display/lookup, never branch on the value itself\" -- because `io_boundary._module_matches` branched on orthography. Its stated reason for why the linter let it stand applies here unchanged: \"a `free-text` justification is required to be **present**, not **true**.\"\n\nSO THIS IS NOT A GATE FAILURE AND NOTHING IS BLOCKED. ADR-0033 §1 is explicit that `free-text` gets \"no value check; the justification was the gate at source-write time\". The gate did its job at write time and the code moved afterwards.\n\nWHY IT STILL MATTERS. ADR-0024 defines `free-text` as \"open-ended payload NO CONSUMER BRANCHES ON\". If consumers branch, the category is wrong by its own definition -- so the fix is NOT to reword the justification to admit branching, which would leave a self-contradictory declaration. ADR-0051 answered the identical question by retiring the axis and declaring a real one (`module-key`). Whether `signature` deserves the same -- a `callable-signature` axis with a per-language grammar catalog, or a narrower declared sub-field for the return type and arity that consumers actually read -- is an ADR-level call, not one to make inside a linker PR. Hence needs_human_review.\n\nCOST OF LEAVING IT: it stops the next reader. It stopped this one. A field that says \"never branch on the value\" is a correct instruction to obey, and obeying it would have blocked WI-fihun's cure (2) outright, since `Symbol.signature` is the ONLY place a Python field's declared type is recorded -- verified on the corpus: field symbols carry exactly three meta keys (visibility_signal 2496, concepts 6, decorators 6) and no declared-type key at all.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that this is the only stale `free-text` justification. The other `free-text` declarations on the core dataclasses were NOT swept -- ADR-0051 fixed its own instance and no family sweep is recorded. That sweep is the natural companion to this row and is not done."  # 9957
    fields:  # 9957
      statement: "Symbol.signature carries a free-text axis justification asserting that no consumer branches on the value, while at least 8 shipped consumers (5 analyzers + jackson_dispatch) parse it for return types and parameter arity; ADR-0024 defines free-text as a payload no consumer branches on, so the category contradicts the code."  # 9957
      root_cause: "A free-text axis justification is checked for PRESENCE, not TRUTH (ADR-0051; ADR-0033 section 1), so the declaration was correct when written and nothing re-checked it as consumers were added."  # 9957
- op: discuss  # 25b7
  at: '2026-09-21T01:20:13Z'  # 25b7
  by: agent  # 25b7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 25b7
  clock: 2  # 25b7
  nonce: 25b7  # 25b7
  message: "RELATED OPEN ROWS, surfaced rather than folded -- each closes on its own repro, and none of them is this one.\n\nSAME DEFECT, ONE REGISTRY OVER:\n  WI-lijaz (todo_hard, P3, [axis]) -- axis_meta_keys.py's docstring states that every meta key is declared there with its axis; measured over 42 cached surveys, 34 of 70 observed keys are unregistered. A declaration contradicted by the shipped code, in the adjacent registry.\n  INV-lafid (violated, P3, [axis]) -- the DETECTOR half: axis_drift.find_drift selects consumers by substring match on the target identifier, so two live io-boundary consumers are invisible by construction. Different axis, same lesson about what the gate cannot see.\n\nTHE PRECEDENT AND ITS QUEUE:\n  WI-livar (done, P1) -- the owner's 2026-09-01 ruling (a) that produced ADR-0051 and the module-key axis. This row's precedent descends from it.\n  WI-marok (todo_hard, P3) -- Phase 2 of that ruling: ADR-0024 step 7, \"migrate violators\". CORRECTION to this row's original NOT ASSERTED paragraph, which said no family sweep is recorded: WI-marok IS the adjacent sweep, but of module-slot PRODUCERS, not of stale free-text justifications on other fields. The claim stands as written; the distinction should not have to be re-derived. Note also that WI-marok is gated behind the v9/v10 id-scheme bumps because external_symbol ids EMBED the module slot -- that gate reason does NOT apply to Symbol.signature, which appears in no id, so a same-shaped ruling here would not queue behind those releases.\n  WI-vusot (todo_hard, P4) -- the ADR-0024 recurrence-promotion review for meta keys, carrying an 8-entry discussion of exactly \"does this need its own ADR, or is it a natural extension of ADR-0024?\". That is the framing question this row escalates.\n\nTHE STRUCTURAL ALTERNATIVE TO PARSING THIS FIELD AT ALL:\n  WI-hudam -> WI-fukut (todo_soft, P4, parent INV-dihos) -- Return-Type Registry for type-annotated Python: a 'signatures' YAML in python.yaml, Tier-2 handling of Optional/Union/pipe syntax, wired into py.py's var_types loop. It would give return types a DECLARED home instead of parsing Symbol.signature, retiring the largest class of this row's eight consumers -- and it is simultaneously WI-fihun cure (1)'s machinery for the Class.factory() shape.\n  WI-gokop (todo_hard, P2) -- the same receiver-typing drain in scala, filed as \"the return-type-registry shape objc and swift already have\". The registry approach is already the house pattern in two languages.\n\nDETECTION:\n  WI-sipuk (todo_hard, P2) -- check-docstring-drift needs a registry-cross-reference sub-check because blame cannot find retired-vocabulary drift. That is the mechanism that would catch the next one of these instead of a human reading a comment.\n\nNO FOLD PROPOSED and no links recorded: different fields, different registries. Surfacing, not performing.\n\nALSO: this row now has a consumer. WI-fihun's cure (2) shipped a ninth value-branching reader of Symbol.signature (method_call_recovery._declares_non_callable_value). That was a deliberate choice, made because ADR-0033 section 1 gives free-text \"no value check\" and ADR-0051 records the justification as \"required to be present, not true\" -- so it is an instance of an existing pattern, not a new liberty. It does make the count nine and strengthens rather than weakens the case here."  # 25b7
