- op: discuss  # fe86
  at: '2026-09-21T06:29:30Z'  # fe86
  by: agent  # fe86
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fe86
  clock: 4  # fe86
  nonce: fe86  # fe86
  message: "CLOSED BY THE OWNER'S A+no RULING (2026-09-21), shipped in PR #1115 (merged 0d53994326) as ADR-0058.\n\nTHE RULING, in the owner's terms: (A) retire the free-text axis and declare a right one; (no) do not widen the parsing further. Both halves shipped.\n\nWHAT LANDED.\n  - `Symbol.signature` declares `# axis: callable-signature` (ir.py:652). The false clause is gone, not reworded -- ADR-0024 defines free-text as a payload NO CONSUMER BRANCHES ON, so admitting branching in the justification would have left a declaration contradicting its own category. ADR-0051's move, one field over.\n  - Registry `hypergumbo_core.signature_axis`: axiom, two notions over three sections, conformance DERIVED from the section (an undeclared name is non-conformant, the direction that cannot manufacture a false all-clear), wired into `_known_axes()`.\n  - `docs/concept-axes.md` renders the axis and a fact-home table; the spec describes it.\n\nTHE \"no\" HALF IS MECHANICAL, NOT A COMMENT. `find_undeclared_value_parsers` walks packages/*/src for `.signature` reads whose value flows into a call and FAILS on any site absent from `LEGACY_VALUE_PARSERS`. The nine are declared there by file:line + anchor, each naming which fact it goes after; a companion test re-checks every citation against the tree. A tenth turns the suite red. That is the ruling made unforgettable rather than written down.\n\nBOTH CONTROLS WERE MUTATION-TESTED rather than assumed: removing the py.py:5881 declaration and rotting a FACT_HOMES anchor each turn the suite red, and both restore green.\n\nCOUNT CORRECTED: the row said 8 in its statement and 9 after cure (2). It is NINE, enumerated in LEGACY_VALUE_PARSERS.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM.\n  - Nothing an analyzer emits changed. The nine still parse. 4.95% of populated signature slots are still a value type on a non-callable. Migration is ADR-0024 step 7, filed as the producer port, and is NOT done.\n  - The producer side has no gate. Nothing stops an analyzer stamping a field's type into `signature` tomorrow; only the consumer side is closed.\n  - Two gate limits are STATED, not covered: a value bound to a local, and a kwarg named `signature`. Neither occurs in the tree; both are written into the module so silence is not read as coverage.\n\nMEASURED FOR THE ADR (survey of this repo, 52,983 symbols): 38,573 carry a signature -- 36,662 callable surfaces, 1,911 (4.95%) a bare value type on a non-callable (1,886 fields + 25 variables; python 1,817, rust 49, typescript 35, then single digits in java/swift/csharp/go/solidity).\n\nA RELATED ROW CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED: `Symbol.docstring` carries a near-identical justification and it is TRUE -- all seven reads in packages/*/src are display, serialisation or `is None` PRESENCE checks, and a presence check is not a value branch. So the clause is not inherently rotten; it goes false when consumers accumulate and nobody re-reads it. ADR-0058 OQ2 records this, and it is the argument for ONE sweep over the remaining 18 free-text declarations on the core dataclasses rather than a fourth one-at-a-time instance. ADR-0051's OQ2 about `ExternalRef.name` is still open and belongs in that sweep. No row moves on this note.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-run on the merged tree (0d53994326) rather than carried from the PR:\n  ir.py:652            -> `# axis: callable-signature` (the free-text clause is gone)\n  find_undeclared_value_parsers(.) -> []   (no undeclared parse site)\n  len(LEGACY_VALUE_PARSERS)        -> 9    (the closed set)\n  'callable-signature' in _known_axes()    -> True\n  notions                          -> ['callable_surface', 'value_type']\nFull affected slice before merge: 677 files, 22,179 passed, 0 failed; both changed modules at 100% coverage; mypy strict ratchet 667 = baseline."  # fe86
